From 44cb713696814aa9d8ce1fecc47139b57f615618 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:01:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(ui): set a tool's holder and stick-out in the tool
 library window

The Tool tab of the tool library window gets an assembly group: the
holder pick, the gauge length, the projection (stick-out), their total,
the shank warning, a taper that is not the machine's spindle mount, and
the refusal of Apply holder before the click. Apply holder is the one
undoable SetToolBody::library. The window keeps its own holder draft.
A change of the stored tool's length re-seeds only the projection draft
(#808 item 2). The preview draws the draft holder.

Refs #808
Fixes #3895

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
