From 9af86ad9f78acef5f71c5975056fabd165e981ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:51:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(ui): judge the Apply holder refusal on the stored
 tool

The assembly group named the Apply holder refusal from the unapplied
tool draft, but SetToolBody::library checks the stored tool. Unapplied
flute edits could hide a real refusal or show a false one. The preview
model now takes the refusal from the stored tool (the key's document
tool) and keeps the draft numbers' verdict as a separate draft note.

Pinned by the_refusal_judges_the_stored_tool_not_shorter_draft_flutes
and longer_draft_flutes_give_a_draft_note_not_an_apply_refusal.

Refs #3895

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
